{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Children not to be penalised for non-attendance due to medical appointments",
        "additional_details": "Medical appointments are essential \u2014 they are not truancy. GP, hospital and dental visits are often unavoidable and cannot always be scheduled outside school hours. Marking these as absences harms a child\u2019s attendance percentage, risks penalties, and creates unnecessary worry for families. Children cannot thrive if their health needs are neglected. The Government must issue robust guidance to ensure that these appointments are excluded from all penalties arising from attendance calculations. No child should be penalised because they need to see a doctor.",
        "background": "Medical appointments are essential healthcare, not truancy. We believe children should not be penalised for GP/hospital/dental visits affecting their attendance. Good health supports learning \u2014 necessary appointments are unavoidable and must not lead to penalties.",
